# Only keys with no code default live here. A default duplicated between this
# file and config.py drifts, and the .env copy silently wins -- so every
# tunable that has a sensible default lives in config.py only.
#
# Copy to .env and fill in. .env is gitignored and must never be committed:
# the remote is public.

# --- Models -----------------------------------------------------------------

# Every LLM role in this project goes through OpenRouter. There is no direct
# OpenAI path: `LLM_PROVIDER` does not exist as a toggle here, unlike in the
# donor projects.
OPENROUTER_API_KEY=

# Per-role model names. All five resolve through OpenRouter.
#
# WHERE THE VALUE ACTUALLY LIVES: config.py's `Settings`, as a default per
# role, written at stage 2 from the model choice stage 1 makes against the
# live OpenRouter catalogue (docs/model-prices-<date>.md). The five lines
# below are OVERRIDES: uncomment one to run a single role on a different
# model without touching code -- useful when comparing two candidates on the
# same golden case. Left commented, each role uses its config.py default,
# and this file cannot drift from that default.
#
# THE CHOSEN VALUES, carried over from MA_systems_hl10 so that a difference
# in results between the two projects is a difference in architecture, not a
# difference in model. hl10 ran all four agent roles on the shared default
# `gpt-4.1-mini` with no per-role override; the same model is addressed as
# `openai/gpt-4.1-mini` on OpenRouter, which is the only provider here.
#
#   MODEL_NAME (shared default for all four agent roles) = openai/gpt-4.1-mini
#
# Stage 2 writes that value into config.py as the default. The four lines
# below stay commented: uncomment one to run a single role on a different
# model without touching code -- useful when comparing two candidates on the
# same golden case.
# MODEL_NAME=
# SUPERVISOR_MODEL_NAME=
# PLANNER_MODEL_NAME=
# RESEARCHER_MODEL_NAME=
# CRITIC_MODEL_NAME=

# The LLM judge used by every DeepEval GEval metric. Unlike the five above,
# this one is NOT commented out: it has no config.py default on purpose, so
# that a judge is always a deliberate choice rather than something inherited
# from whatever the agents happen to run. Resolved on OpenRouter like every
# other role. Two requirements, both checked at startup:
#   1. the model must honour strict structured output, or GEval returns no
#      score at all -- models.assert_structured_output_supported refuses and
#      names the model;
#   2. it should come from a different model family than the agent roles, to
#      avoid self-preference bias.
# The second is a precaution, not a proven property: this project does not
# validate the judge against human labels, so its scores are a signal for
# where to look, not measured truth. Filled in at stage 1 from the live
# OpenRouter catalogue -- unless the hl10 choice is kept, which it is by
# default here:
#
#   JUDGE_MODEL_NAME=google/gemini-2.5-pro
#
# hl10 measured this one against a cheaper candidate and kept it. That
# measurement does not transfer to this project (different agents, different
# rubric, and no judge validation here at all), so it is carried as a
# reasonable starting point, not as a validated result. It does satisfy the
# family-independence precaution: Gemini is not the family running the
# agents.
JUDGE_MODEL_NAME=

# --- Embeddings -------------------------------------------------------------

# CORRECTED AT STAGE 2 (see insights.md, "Mistake" entries dated 2026-08-22):
# an earlier finding claimed OpenRouter had no embeddings endpoint. That was
# wrong -- `POST /api/v1/embeddings` works and serves
# `openai/text-embedding-3-small`, verified live (1536 dims). Embeddings run
# through OpenRouter, the same as every other role in this project, and the
# index is directly comparable with hl10's -- no second provider, no
# `OPENAI_API_KEY`.
#
#   EMBEDDING_PROVIDER = openrouter (config.py default; this line is the
#                         override point, left commented)
#   EMBEDDING_MODEL     = openai/text-embedding-3-small (config.py default)
#
# `local` remains a real toggle value -- the documented offline escape hatch
# via a Hugging Face model -- but is no longer the default.
# EMBEDDING_PROVIDER=local

# Keep the model cache off the system drive. Without it, sentence-transformers
# downloads a few hundred megabytes into C:\Users\...\.cache and never asks.
#
# READ THIS BEFORE TRUSTING THE LINES BELOW. `.env` is parsed by
# pydantic-settings into `Settings`; it is NOT exported into the process
# environment. Hugging Face and pip read `os.environ` and nothing else, so
# these values take effect only once config.py writes them there at import
# time -- the same shape hl10 used to make its tracing flags reach an SDK
# that only reads os.environ. Until stage 2 does that, the ambient
# environment wins.
#
# Measured on this machine, 2026-08-22: the ambient environment already sets
# HF_HOME=F:\hf-cache, and pip's own config points at f:\pip-cache. Both are
# off the system drive, so the requirement is currently met by accident --
# which is exactly why it is written down rather than assumed to hold on the
# next machine.
HF_HOME=.cache/hf
PIP_CACHE_DIR=.cache/pip

# --- Tracing (stage 5) ------------------------------------------------------

# This project's own switch, not a Langfuse variable -- Langfuse itself is
# configured by the three LANGFUSE_* keys below and by nothing else.
#
# Accepted values: `true` / `false`. Unset means false, so tracing is off
# until someone turns it on deliberately. Every gate test and every run of
# the system passes with it off.
#
# `true` without BOTH Langfuse keys below is refused at startup, not
# attempted: a refused request is far easier to diagnose than a background
# exporter thread failing silently on every span.
#
# In hl10 this had to be an explicit `true`: with it unset, nothing was
# exported at all and Langfuse simply showed no traces -- which reads from the
# UI exactly like "Langfuse refuses to accept them". If traces are missing at
# stage 5, check this line before debugging anything else.
#
# Leave it empty until stage 5, when observability.py exists to read it --
# setting it now has no reader. The keys below can be filled in already.
TRACING_ENABLED=

# Langfuse Cloud. This project has no docker-compose.yml and no self-hosted
# Langfuse: the v3 stack needs roughly 5.5 GB of container memory, which this
# machine does not have. Keys are created in the Langfuse Cloud UI.
#
# Traces carry system prompts, corpus excerpts, user questions and model
# answers to an external service. That is accepted here because the corpus is
# public research papers -- see CONTRIBUTING.md, "What leaves this machine".
LANGFUSE_PUBLIC_KEY=
LANGFUSE_SECRET_KEY=
LANGFUSE_BASE_URL=https://cloud.langfuse.com

# --- Evaluation tooling -----------------------------------------------------

# DeepEval phones home with anonymous usage telemetry unless this is set.
# With it set, no telemetry file is written at all (measured, stage 7
# kickoff) -- DEEPEVAL_HOME below then never actually matters, but is
# still redirected into .cache/ by config.py so the invariant holds even
# if telemetry is ever turned back on.
DEEPEVAL_TELEMETRY_OPT_OUT=YES

# Exported into os.environ by config.py's _CacheSettings, the same shape
# as HF_HOME/PIP_CACHE_DIR above -- not read here directly.
DEEPEVAL_HOME=.cache/deepeval
